convertible-power (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The GDM login screen no longer suspends from inactivity on AC power
    (/usr/share/gdm/dconf/95-convertible-power). GNOME's greeter default is to
    suspend after 15 minutes idle even on AC, so a laptop left at the login
    screen after a reboot went to sleep and dropped off the network (bruce17).

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:10:00 -0800

convertible-power (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop a still-running power-profiles-daemon when configuring: TLP will not set
    the CPU boost or energy settings while it runs, and removing the package
    did not always stop it (seen on a CF-19, where battery mode left turbo on).

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700

convertible-power (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Do not disable wake-on-LAN (WOL_DISABLE=N): TLP's default turned it off, which
    stopped a suspended CF-19 being woken remotely.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700

convertible-power (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: TLP settings (AC = performance, battery = efficiency),
    UPower critical action at 10%, and convertible-battery-notify, a reminder
    to unplug at 80% for firmware without a charge limit.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:30:00 -0700
